# The gnu interpreter's direct dependencies - the kernel stack only; the musl image's
# requirements.in carries the server's, and a Space's own `%pip install` brings
# everything else from PyPI as released. requirements-gnu.lock is compiled from this file
# and holds every transitive package with the sha256 of every manylinux wheel; the
# Dockerfile installs it with --require-hashes.
#
# Recompile from this directory (the header of requirements-gnu.lock records the command).

# The kernel and its entry point (jupydroid_kernel.py).
ipykernel==7.3.0
